The steady state distribution of a queue is the distribution 
\emph on 
stationary distribution
\emph default 
 that the Markov chain converges to.
 It occurs when a 
\emph on 
dynamic equilibrium
\emph default 
 is obtained in the queueing system.
 A dynamic equilibrium is when change in one direction is balanced (on average)
 by change in the opposite direction.
 The steady state distribution is
\emph on 
 used for making predictions 
\emph default 
about the expected states of the queue.
