answer{
\end_inset 

Kleinrock's independence assumption is an assumption that a packets service
 time at a node in a network of queues is statistically independent of its
 service time at any other node in the queueing model.

\series bold 
\emph on 
 
\series default 
\emph default 
In the approximation you assume each communication link is an 
\begin_inset Formula $M/M/1$
\end_inset 


\series bold 
\emph on 
 
