Give conditions under which Kleinrock's independence assumption will yield
 a reasonable approximation for a network of queues.
\begin_deeper 
\layout Mypercent

25
\end_deeper 
\layout Standard

\SpecialChar ~

\begin_inset ERT
status Collapsed

\layout Standard

\backslash 
answer{
\end_inset 

Kleinrock suggested that when different traffic streams are merged to form
 a single stream the approximation becomes reasonable.
 Particularly if that traffic is a large volume from outside the network
 and is Poisson distributed.
 The approximation also is better for single path routing algorithms.
 (Example 3.17 in Bertsekas and Gallagher) 
